    "titulo": "You can be below the average 401(k) and still beat most people your age",
    "descripcion": "Vanguard's How America Saves 2026 puts the average 401(k) balance for participants 65 and older at $330,186, while the median is $103,202. A few very large accounts pull the average up: across all ages the $167,970 average lands near the 75th percentile, so about three in four participants hold less. Being above the median doesn't mean you're done: that balance alone won't fund most retirements, and these figures exclude IRAs, pensions, home equity and Social Security. Vanguard's plans also lean toward larger employers. Not financial advice.",
